Subject: [PATCH] Fig. 2f: wave-bounded bars with ray-optics marks

A +-2 mrad tilt of the 40 um launch stays inside the beam divergence
(7.9 mrad), so wave optics keeps the angle-dither factor >= 0.98. Panel
(f) now shows, per layout, angle = max(ray value, 0.98 x no dither) and
both = max(ray value, 0.98 x wavelength only), with medians and
quartiles over the 30 layouts; black marks give the ray-optics medians
(the earlier bars). The rail selects wave+ray (default), wave only or
ray only; the ensemble table and the settings file carry the
wave-bounded values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NLfEqncaEw1RGMDLUGdFgb
